       "text": "I won't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily. The reason you gave is about timing and the family visit, not a clinical need for this dose. At five times the maximum dose, the risk of serious harm to a 70 kg patient with normal organ function is high. Nothing about this patient makes that dose safe.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. If you need more blood pressure control, I can add a second agent from a different class.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily**, with titration over 1 to 2 weeks.\n- **Enter the order with a note** asking for pharmacist review, if you have a documented reason for an unusual dose. Please give me the clinical rationale.\n\nIf the aim is to have everything settled before evening rounds, I can enter an appropriate order now. Tell me which dose you want and I'll do it."
